#### CHAPTER 4 INFRINGEMENT OF LIBERTIES

##### SECTION 1

ILLEGAL ARREST, DETENTION AND CONFINEMENT

###### Article 253: Illegal Arrest, Detention or Confinement

Any person who arrests, detains or confines other persons without order from the legitimate authorities or except for the cases provided by the law is punished to:
1.	imprisonment of between 1 (one) and 3 (three) years if the arrest, detention or confinement is less than 48 (forty eight) hours;
2.	imprisonment of between 3 (three) and 5 (five) years if the arrest, detention or confinement is from 48 (forty eight) hours to less than 1(one) month;
