###### Article 278: Corruption Committed by an Employee

The acts committed by an employee to solicit or accept a gift, a present, a promise or any benefit to perform or not perform his/her duty without the knowledge of the employer and without his/her consent, is punishable for an imprisonment of between 6 (six) months and 2 (two) years and a fine of between 1,000,000 (one million) Riels and 4,000,000 (four million) Riels.

###### Article 279: Bribes Given to an Employee

Any person who hands over an employee any gift, present, makes a promise to him/her or provides him/her with any benefit in order for the latter to perform or to abstain from performing his/her duty, without the knowledge of the employer and without his/her consent, is punishable for an imprisonment of between 6 (six) months and 2 (two) years and a fine of between 1,000,000 (one million) Riels and 4,000,000 (four million) Riels.

