###### Article 372: Blackmail

##### SECTION 3 BLACKMAIL

The blackmail is an act of obtaining, by means of threatening to disclose or to impute facts so as knowingly to ruin a person's honour or friendship:
1.	a signature;

2.	a commitment or a renunciation;
3.	the disclosure of a secret;
4.	the delivery of funds, of assets or any property.

###### Article 373: Penalties to be Imposed

Blackmail is punishable by an imprisonment from 2 (two) years to 5 (five) years and a fine from 4,000,000 (four million) Riels to 10,000,000 (ten million) Riels.

###### Article 374: Aggravating Circumstances based on Practical Application of Blackmail

When the blackmail to disclose or to impute facts to ruin a person's honour or friendship is carried out, the perpetrator is punished to an imprisonment from 5 (five) and 10 (ten) years.

###### Article 375: Attempt

